// ============================================================================
//  ID:             Q08  (report appendix: A6)
//  Name:           Did any monitoring service actually stop
//  Purpose:        Check whether the attacker's stop commands ran, and whether the services stayed up.
//  Hunt step:      11
//  ATT&CK:         T1562.001 Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools (attempted)
//  Tables:         HartwellSysmon_CL
//  Time range:     2026-10-23 04:00 to 16:00 UTC
//  Environment:    Practice lab
//  Hit looks like: "systemctl stop" commands from www-data against monitoring services.
//  Result:         The stop attempts failed. The attacker's own "systemctl is-active" check showed
//                  all three services still running.
//  Benign noise:   Legitimate administrator maintenance, which would run as another account.
//  Tuning notes:   Pair with a check that the services kept logging (the narrative in the report
//                  relies on this). That check is not saved here.
//  Changed from the report: the www-data filter used typographic quotes, a syntax error. Replaced
//                  with straight quotes.
//  Author / date:  Cai Spice · hunt run 2026-10-23, documented 2026-11-20
// ============================================================================

HartwellSysmon_CL
| where OriginalTime between (datetime(2026-10-23T04:00:00Z) .. datetime(2026-10-23T16:00:00Z))
| where User == "www-data"
| where CommandLine contains "systemctl stop"
| project OriginalTime, CommandLine, Image
